title: binary ninja il (llil mlil hlil)
url:   https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html
tags:  binaryninja binja bn python api il bnil llil mlil hlil ssa intermediate-language decompiler dataflow

; i = an IL instruction (any level), il = an IL function. UPPERCASE words are placeholders.
; Guide: https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/bnil-overview.html

## get il functions
f.llil / f.mlil / f.hlil     # get the Low, Medium or High Level IL of a function  @bnil  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.function-module.html#binaryninja.function.Function.hlil>
f.lifted_il                  # get the lifted IL (LLIL before flag and stack cleanup)  @lift @raw  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.function-module.html#binaryninja.function.Function.lifted_il>
f.mmlil                      # get the mapped MLIL (keeps stores that MLIL drops)  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.function-module.html#binaryninja.function.Function.mmlil>
il.ssa_form                  # get the SSA form of an IL function  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.ssa_form>
il.non_ssa_form              # get the normal form back from an SSA IL function  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.non_ssa_form>
il.source_function           # get the Function an IL function belongs to  @owner  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.source_function>
il.llil / il.mlil / il.hlil  # move between IL levels of the same function  @map @level  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.hlil>
il.view / il.arch            # get the BinaryView and Architecture of an IL function  @bv  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.view>
str(f.hlil)                  # print the whole decompiled function  @decompile @text  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILFunction>
f.hlil.root                  # get the top HLIL instruction (the function body block)  @ast @tree  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILFunction.root>

## walk instructions
il.instructions           # iterate every top-level IL instruction of a function  @loop  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.instructions>
for bb in il:             # iterate the IL basic blocks of a function  @loop  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction>
for i in bb:              # iterate the instructions of an IL basic block  @loop  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILBasicBlock>
il[N]                     # get instruction number N (an instruction index)  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction>
len(il)                   # count the top-level instructions  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction>
bv.hlil_instructions      # iterate every HLIL instruction in the whole binary  @all @global  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.hlil_instructions>
il.traverse(CB)           # walk every instruction and sub-expression, yield what CB returns (non None)  @find  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.traverse>
    def find_consts(i):
        if isinstance(i, Constant):
            return i.constant
    print(list(current_mlil.traverse(find_consts)))
i.traverse(CB, ARGS...)   # walk one instruction's expression tree depth-first, yield CB results  @recursive  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.traverse>
i.visit(CB)               # call CB(name, inst, type, parent) on each sub-instruction; return False to stop going deeper  @walk  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.visit>
i.visit_operands(CB)      # call CB on every leaf operand (vars, constants...)  @walk  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.visit_operands>
i.prefix_operands / i.postfix_operands  # list all operands of the tree in prefix / postfix order  @flatten  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.prefix_operands>
il.get_basic_block_at(N)  # get the IL block that holds instruction N  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_basic_block_at>
il.get_expr(EXPR_INDEX)   # get an IL expression by expression index  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_expr>
il.get_expr_count()       # count all expressions in the IL function  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_expr_count>

## instruction basics
i.operation          # get the operation enum, e.g. MediumLevelILOperation.MLIL_CALL  @op @opcode @kind  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.operation>
i.operation.name     # get the operation name as text, e.g. "HLIL_ASSIGN"  @op  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.operation>
i.address            # get the assembly address this IL came from (approximate)  @addr @location  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.address>
i.size               # get the result size in bytes  @width  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.size>
i.instr_index        # get the index of the top-level instruction that holds this expression  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction>
i.expr_index         # get the expression index inside the IL function  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction>
i.function           # get the IL function that owns the instruction  @owner  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction>
i.il_basic_block     # get the IL block that holds the instruction  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.il_basic_block>
i.operands           # list the operands (sub-expressions, vars, ints...)  @args @children  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.operands>
i.detailed_operands  # list (name, value, type) for each operand  @args @names @debug  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.detailed_operands>
i.tokens             # get the instruction as text tokens  @render  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.tokens>
str(i)               # get the instruction as text  @render @print  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction>
i.lines              # get the HLIL text lines of an instruction (HLIL only)  @render  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILInstruction.lines>
i.expr_type          # get the Type of an MLIL/HLIL expression  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.expr_type>
i.attributes         # get the set of ILInstructionAttribute flags on an instruction  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.attributes>
i.parent             # get the parent expression in the HLIL tree  @ast @up  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILInstruction.parent>
i.instr              # get the HLIL statement that holds an expression  @ast  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILInstruction.instr>
i.has_side_effects   # check whether an HLIL expression has side effects  @pure  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILInstruction.has_side_effects>
MediumLevelILInstruction.show_mlil_hierarchy()  # open a graph of all MLIL classes (also show_llil_ / show_hlil_hierarchy)  @learn  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.show_mlil_hierarchy>

## match by kind
isinstance(i, Call)               # match any call at any level (commonil class)  @filter  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Call>
isinstance(i, Localcall) / isinstance(i, Tailcall) / isinstance(i, Syscall)  # match normal calls, tail calls or syscalls  @call  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Localcall>
isinstance(i, Constant)           # match any constant expression  @const @immediate  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Constant>
isinstance(i, BinaryOperation) / isinstance(i, UnaryOperation)  # match two-operand or one-operand math  @arith  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.BinaryOperation>
isinstance(i, Comparison)         # match compare expressions (==, <, ...)  @cmp @condition  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Comparison>
isinstance(i, Load) / isinstance(i, Store)  # match memory reads / writes  @deref  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Load>
isinstance(i, SetVar)             # match variable assignments  @assign  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.SetVar>
isinstance(i, Return) / isinstance(i, Terminal)  # match returns / block-ending instructions  @ret  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Return>
isinstance(i, ControlFlow) / isinstance(i, Loop)  # match branches, ifs, loops  @flow  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.ControlFlow>
isinstance(i, Phi)                # match SSA phi nodes  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Phi>
isinstance(i, Intrinsic)          # match CPU intrinsics  @builtin  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.Intrinsic>
isinstance(i, FloatingPoint)      # match float operations  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.FloatingPoint>
isinstance(i, MediumLevelILCall)  # match one exact operation class  @call @mlil  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILCall>
i.operation == HighLevelILOperation.HLIL_CALL  # match one exact operation by enum  @op  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILInstruction.operation>
match i: case HighLevelILCall(dest=HighLevelILConstPtr(constant=ADDR)):  # pattern-match IL with keyword patterns (Python 3.10+)  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILCall>
    match i:
        case HighLevelILCall(dest=HighLevelILConstPtr(constant=c), params=[_, n, *_]):
            print(hex(c), n)
        case HighLevelILAssign(dest=HighLevelILVar(var=v)):
            print("write", v)

## common operands
call.dest / call.params               # get a call's target and argument list  @args @arguments  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILCall>
call.output                           # list the variables a MLIL call writes  @return  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILCall.output>
set_var.dest / set_var.src            # get the target variable and value of an MLIL assignment  @assign  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILSetVar>
assign.dest / assign.src              # get both sides of an HLIL assignment (also HLIL_VAR_INIT)  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILAssign>
if_.condition / if_.true / if_.false  # get an if's condition and both targets/bodies  @branch  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILIf>
load.src                              # get the address expression of a memory read  @deref  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILLoad>
store.dest / store.src                # get the address and value of a memory write  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILStore>
const.constant                        # get the integer of a constant or constant pointer  @immediate @value  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILConstPtr>
const_ptr.string                      # get (text, StringType) if a constant pointer points at a string  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILConstPtr>
var_expr.var / var_expr.src           # get the Variable read by a var expression (src on MLIL, var on HLIL)  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILVar>
binop.left / binop.right              # get both sides of a binary operation  @math @operands  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.BinaryOperation>
unop.src                              # get the operand of a unary operation (neg, not, zx, sx, deref...)  @math  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.commonil-module.html#binaryninja.commonil.UnaryOperation>
ret.src                               # list the returned values  @return  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILRet>
jump_to.dest / jump_to.targets        # get a switch jump's address and dict of case -> target  @jumptable  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILJumpTo>
deref_field.src / .offset / .member_index  # get the base, byte offset and member of HLIL p->field  @struct  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILDerefField>
struct_field.src / .offset            # get the base and offset of HLIL s.field  @member  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILStructField>
array_index.src / array_index.index   # get the array and index of HLIL a[i]  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILArrayIndex>
loop.condition / loop.body            # get a while/do-while loop's test and body  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILWhile>
for_.init / .condition / .update / .body  # get the parts of an HLIL for loop  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILFor>
switch.condition / switch.cases / switch.default  # get the parts of an HLIL switch  @case  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILSwitch>
addr_of.src                           # get the variable whose address is taken (&var)  @pointer  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILAddressOf>
intrinsic.intrinsic / intrinsic.params  # get an intrinsic's ILIntrinsic and its arguments  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILIntrinsic>
llil_set_reg.dest / llil_set_reg.src  # get the register and value of an LLIL register write  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILSetReg>
llil_reg.src.name                     # get the register name read by LLIL_REG  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.ILRegister.name>

## variables in il
i.vars_read / i.vars_written          # list variables an instruction reads / writes  @uses @defs @dataflow  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.vars_read>
i.vars_address_taken                  # list variables whose address the instruction takes  @alias  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.vars_address_taken>
il.vars                               # list variables used in this IL function  @locals  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.vars>
il.aliased_vars                       # list variables whose address is taken and used elsewhere  @alias @pointer  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.aliased_vars>
il.get_var_definitions(VAR)           # list instructions that assign a variable  @defs @dataflow  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_var_definitions>
il.get_var_uses(VAR)                  # list instructions that read a variable  @dataflow  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_var_uses>
il.is_var_live_at(VAR, INSTR)         # check whether a variable is live at an instruction  @liveness  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.is_var_live_at>
il.get_live_instructions_for_var(VAR)  # list instructions where a variable is live  @liveness  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_live_instructions_for_var>
i.get_var_for_reg("rdi")              # get the MLIL variable that holds a register at an instruction  @map  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.get_var_for_reg>
i.get_var_for_stack_location(OFFSET)  # get the MLIL variable at a stack offset at an instruction  @map  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.get_var_for_stack_location>

## ssa
il.ssa_form                           # get the SSA version of the IL  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.ssa_form>
i.ssa_form / i.non_ssa_form           # move one instruction into or out of SSA form  @map  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.ssa_form>
ssa_var.var / ssa_var.version         # get the Variable and version of an SSAVariable  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.SSAVariable>
il.ssa_vars                           # list SSAVariables of the function  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.ssa_vars>
il.ssa_form.get_ssa_var_definition(SSA_VAR)  # get the one instruction that defines an SSA variable  @def @source  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_ssa_var_definition>
il.ssa_form.get_ssa_var_uses(SSA_VAR)  # list instructions that use an SSA variable  @sink  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_ssa_var_uses>
ssa_var.def_site / ssa_var.use_sites  # get the definition / uses straight from an SSAVariable  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.SSAVariable.def_site>
    arg = call.params[0].ssa_form            # <mlil: x0#3>
    d = arg.function.get_ssa_var_definition(arg.src)
    # if d is a phi (MediumLevelILVarPhi), follow each d.src version in a worklist
il.get_ssa_var_value(SSA_VAR)         # get the RegisterValue analysis found for an SSA variable  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_ssa_var_value>
il.is_ssa_var_live(SSA_VAR)           # check whether an SSA variable is used at all  @dead  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.is_ssa_var_live>
i.ssa_memory_version                  # get the memory version at an SSA instruction  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.ssa_memory_version>
il.get_ssa_memory_definition(VERSION)  # get the instruction that makes a memory version  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_ssa_memory_definition>
llil.ssa_form.get_ssa_reg_definition(SSA_REG)  # get the LLIL instruction that defines an SSA register  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILFunction.get_ssa_reg_definition>
llil.ssa_form.get_ssa_reg_uses(SSA_REG)  # list LLIL instructions that use an SSA register  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILFunction.get_ssa_reg_uses>
llil.ssa_form.get_ssa_flag_definition(SSA_FLAG)  # get the LLIL instruction that sets an SSA flag  @flags  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILFunction.get_ssa_flag_definition>

## map between levels
i.llil / i.mlil / i.hlil        # map an instruction to the closest one at another level (may be None)  @translate  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.hlil>
i.llils / i.mlils / i.hlils     # list all instructions at another level that make up this one (more exact)  @map  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.highlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.highlevelil.HighLevelILInstruction.mlils>
i.mmlil                         # map LLIL to the mapped MLIL  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILInstruction.mmlil>
f.get_llil_at(ADDR).hlil        # find the HLIL for an assembly address  @lookup  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.function-module.html#binaryninja.function.Function.get_llil_at>
f.get_llils_at(ADDR)            # list LLIL instructions for an address (one address can lift to many)  @lookup  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.function-module.html#binaryninja.function.Function.get_llils_at>
llil.get_instructions_at(ADDR)  # list LLIL instruction indexes for an address  @lookup @index  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILFunction.get_instructions_at>
il.get_instruction_start(ADDR)  # get the first IL instruction index for an address  @lookup  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_instruction_start>
mlil.get_low_level_il_instruction_index(N)  # map an MLIL instruction index to LLIL  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_low_level_il_instruction_index>
mlil.get_high_level_il_instruction_index(N)  # map an MLIL instruction index to HLIL  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.get_high_level_il_instruction_index>
ref.hlil                        # get the HLIL at a cross reference (ReferenceSource)  @xrefs  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.ReferenceSource.hlil>

## values and dataflow
i.value                             # get the RegisterValue analysis found for an expression  @constant @dataflow  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.value>
i.value.type == RegisterValueType.ConstantValue  # check whether an expression is a known constant  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.variable-module.html#binaryninja.variable.RegisterValue>
i.possible_values                   # get the PossibleValueSet (ranges, sets, tables) of an expression  @range @dataflow  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.possible_values>
pvs.type / pvs.value / pvs.ranges / pvs.values  # read the kind and contents of a PossibleValueSet  @range @set  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.variable-module.html#binaryninja.variable.PossibleValueSet>
i.get_reg_value("rax")              # get a register value at an instruction  @dataflow  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.get_reg_value>
i.get_possible_reg_values_after("rax")  # get the possible values of a register after an instruction  @range  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.get_possible_reg_values_after>
i.get_stack_contents(OFFSET, SIZE)  # get the value of a stack slot at an instruction  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.get_stack_contents>
i.get_flag_value("z")               # get a flag value at an LLIL/MLIL instruction  @flags  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILInstruction.get_flag_value>
i.branch_dependence                 # get which branch sides must be taken to reach an MLIL instruction  @control-dependence  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILInstruction.branch_dependence>
PossibleValueSet.constant(5)        # make a constant value set (also unsigned_range_value, in_set_of_values...)  @create  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.variable-module.html#binaryninja.variable.PossibleValueSet.constant>
bv.parse_possiblevalueset("[0x10, 0x20]", RegisterValueType.UnsignedRangeValue)  # build a value set from text  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.parse_possiblevalueset>

## llil specifics
llil.regs / llil.flags             # list registers / flags used in an LLIL function  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILFunction.regs>
llil.ssa_regs                      # list SSA registers with versions  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILFunction.ssa_regs>
ILRegister.name / ILRegister.temp  # get a register's name and whether it is an IL temp  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.ILRegister>
i.flags                            # get the flag write type of an LLIL instruction (which flags it sets)  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILInstruction.flags>
LowLevelILFlagCondition.LLFC_E     # name a flag condition (E, NE, SLT, ULT, ...) in LLIL_FLAG_COND  @flags  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.enums-module.html>
llil.get_exits_for_instr(N)        # list exit points for an LLIL instruction index  @flow  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.lowlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.lowlevelil.LowLevelILFunction.get_exits_for_instr>

## graphs
il.create_graph()  # build a FlowGraph of the IL function  @cfg  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mediumlevelil-module.html#binaryninja.mediumlevelil.MediumLevelILFunction.create_graph>
show_graph_report("MLIL", f.mlil.create_graph())  # show an IL graph in a new tab  @ui  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.interaction-module.html#binaryninja.interaction.show_graph_report>
f.create_graph(FunctionGraphType.HighLevelILFunctionGraph)  # build a FlowGraph for a chosen IL view  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.function-module.html#binaryninja.function.Function.create_graph>
